{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612059} {:answer/id #uuid "e95be933-f6de-54d2-9ee9-c0b06be03a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612197} {:answer/id #uuid "eab022ad-201c-57e8-8233-33e117794c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612204} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc4b9da-46fb-5279-9786-ecb80bb26851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eab022ad-201c-57e8-8233-33e117794c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612204} :answer-field/id #uuid "f039dd94-26d0-5900-a8b2-53677ec4ac5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c7554324-4396-5977-8641-f195dcabf7e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74199" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -10\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -10 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(C).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "362c7b53-e5ab-54b0-9fe0-38a925dae292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611817} {:answer/id #uuid "45605044-f69e-5a53-98b8-5835cbeedc77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611846} {:answer/id #uuid "59b4dbed-fa40-578d-9a72-4e6b9b0f0cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611890} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4ecfd5-9072-5e1b-bfae-e86e0b2facab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(G)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612095} {:answer/id #uuid "c35ff534-9d54-5c5b-a7a9-7efe33e36024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c35ff534-9d54-5c5b-a7a9-7efe33e36024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612106} :answer-field/id #uuid "adfaf61e-d071-5834-aced-32711671aa03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e956392f-f2d4-58db-acf4-db7f97c344ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-35560" :question/problem "The matrix $G$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(G).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{g}_{1}+{x}_{2}{g}_{2},$ and ${g}_{1}$, ${g}_{2}$, and ${g}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $G.$\n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(G),$ we need to check if the equation $Gx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[G\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[G\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -1 & -30\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ -10{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=-30.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and we have one free variable ${x}_{3}.$ From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=3-\\frac{1}{10}{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nand from the first one, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=8-3{x}_{2}=-1+\\frac{3}{10}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=-1+\\frac{3}{10}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=3-\\frac{1}{10}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} &={x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $Gx=b$ is consistent which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(G).$ Since we are interested in writing $b$ as $b={x}_{1}{g}_{1}+{x}_{2}{g}_{2}$, that is to say, as a linear combination of the first two columns, then we need to set ${x}_{3}=0.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}=(-1)\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{{g}_{1}}+3\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{{g}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-1)\\cdot 3=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186630938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19fdcdad-0af9-5abb-9ab9-caca78f3706b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630477} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd46735-721a-5bc2-ab9f-d4cb94bafb7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630509} {:answer/id #uuid "70a2b262-1de7-5d68-b597-cf7cf53fc2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630593} {:answer/id #uuid "7332819a-aac6-5026-8e05-9e1b4b3ff2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630598} {:answer/id #uuid "8f9c0bd7-be21-5102-9c1b-8c8eb4686370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(G)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19fdcdad-0af9-5abb-9ab9-caca78f3706b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630477} :answer-field/id #uuid "273e04d9-eee6-53c8-95b5-e83883884446" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "52c37c2b-100a-5a93-b414-8165626049ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-35565" :question/problem "The matrix $G$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(G).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{g}_{1}+{x}_{2}{g}_{2},$ and ${g}_{1}$, ${g}_{2}$, and ${g}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $G.$\n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(G),$ we need to check if the equation $Gx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[G\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[G\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -7 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-2-2{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nand from the first one, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =1-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =1-2(-2-2{x}_{3})-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5+{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=5+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-2-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} &={x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $Gx=b$ is consistent which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(G).$ Since we are interested in writing $b$ as $b={x}_{1}{g}_{1}+{x}_{2}{g}_{2}$, that is to say, as a linear combination of the first two columns, then we need to set ${x}_{3}=0.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}=5\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{{g}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{{g}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=5\\cdot (-2)=-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186630980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "994976f1-6abf-5404-86e4-0ed8d2e09b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630665} {:answer/id #uuid "a99aa545-f503-5c31-b19f-6e7eda5e1edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630687} {:answer/id #uuid "c22790c3-fa8e-5a61-9e9e-599e058b407d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630722} {:answer/id #uuid "c310f952-f342-5f6e-92bd-6664a6077e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630723} {:answer/id #uuid "c7346fb9-7337-5cb5-a324-8eda51142211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a99aa545-f503-5c31-b19f-6e7eda5e1edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630687} :answer-field/id #uuid "da7744ae-0248-574e-bc3e-4ded4edf9a27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cb6b66ec-802b-59dd-8255-547f4504170d" :question/math-academy-id "q-111043" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -4 & 1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -7 & -2 & -1 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -4 & 1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -7 & -2 & -1 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -4 & 1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & -2 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -4 & 1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4} &=-6 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4} &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the  third equation, we get a false statement $0=10.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186630988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08832b58-aab7-5d8c-94c9-ec265ff97462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630441} {:answer/id #uuid "182946eb-5158-5099-a2d2-541682965d02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630472} {:answer/id #uuid "8225becf-6cbb-5c51-9cff-41ce140d72dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630621} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9dca6c-7ba1-5623-bbcc-47f100fd6c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630755} {:answer/id #uuid "edba26e5-d40b-5268-99bc-66f467a0684e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8225becf-6cbb-5c51-9cff-41ce140d72dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630621} :answer-field/id #uuid "c57decc1-6432-5509-8677-d8c8117ae9f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e6a50dbb-3724-5039-86c0-7cadda4d9271" :question/math-academy-id "q-74219" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $H=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ k+1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(H).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(H),$ then the equation $Hx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[H\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[H\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & k+1 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & k+1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & k+1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3k-1 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & k+1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3k-1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6k+7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & k+1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3k-1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3k+6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=k+1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-3k-1 \\\\ 0 &=3k+6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=3k+6,$ which means that $k=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc86e43-9745-591f-9588-4caded67ab87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669507} {:answer/id #uuid "47430476-dff6-52f4-be74-7f5b8e0c8b2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669578} {:answer/id #uuid "98331b42-97d5-5f08-9a57-1c1d99e06e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669712} {:answer/id #uuid "c017e233-a4df-5e9e-9abd-7072a64e95e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669774} {:answer/id #uuid "cbaa8c22-a575-5410-ac83-a109e4be7452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98331b42-97d5-5f08-9a57-1c1d99e06e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669712} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d95780-1583-57c8-8f07-a62ede3cf188" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "54ab4f7c-03e1-5479-9e1c-2b41efbd9755" :question/math-academy-id "q-110961" :question/problem "The matrix $F$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{f}_{1}+{x}_{2}{f}_{2},$ and ${f}_{1},$  ${f}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $F.$\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(F),$ we need to check if the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[F\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[F\\,|\\,b] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -7 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{2} &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=4.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=5.$  \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}=5\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{{f}_{1}}+4\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}_{{f}_{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=5\\cdot 4=20.$"}]}
